  "question": {
    "text": "The circuit contains two diodes each with a forward resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and with infinite reverse resistance. If the battery voltage is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>, the current through the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistance is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0126_03cd9c841692.png\" style=\"width: 179px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0126_27435736828a.png\" style=\"width: 206px; height: 169px;\" /></p><p>In this circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> will be forward bias and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;will be revers bias.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> There will be no current through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Apply KVL in circuit we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>130</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>120</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p>"
  }
}